#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9725 expect=skipped domain=PP
#note "EXACTLY ONE of the pair is present: PPENINT exists (PPSTINT does not), so Requirements.Variables.None [--STINT, --ENINT] skips this sister -- the ruling scoped it to NEITHER-exists only, because FDA-SD1450/SD1451 already report the one-of-two cases over CV/EG/PP/RE and a broader sister would duplicate them (R-5.26). The parent FDA-SD1348 also skips here (its All gate wants both columns), which is exactly the division of labour the ruling records: one-of-two belongs to SD1450/SD1451, neither-of-two to this sister."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
col PPTEST   type=Char label="Parameter Name"
col PPENINT  type=Char label="Planned End of Assessment Interval"
---
S1 | PP | 001 | 1 | AUCINT | AUC from T1 to T2 | PT12H
